---
title: Chicken Bibimbap
description: This Chicken Bibimbap is flavor-packed and makes a perfect lunch or dinner to share with a friend. You’ll start by tossing chicken in an easy garlic-soy marinade that will ensure your chicken is crisp and caramelized when you cook it. Then, you’ll keep building the dish with cooked carrots, spinach, and shiitake mushrooms. Fry up a couple of eggs and you’re ready to serve a delicious meal.
author: Katie Aubin
cook time: 30 minutes
cuisine: Asian
source: https://tasty.co/recipe/chicken-bibimbap
prep time: 30 minutes
time required: 1 hour
servings: 2
course: Dinner
---

In a #shallow dish{}, combine @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @ginger{2%teaspoons}(minced),
@scallions{2}(thinly sliced), @soy sauce{¼%cup}, @sesame oil{2%tablespoons},
@mirin{1%tablespoon}, and @light brown sugar{1%tablespoon}, and whisk to combine.

Add the @chicken thighs{1%lb}(boneless, skinless, sliced into 1/2 inch strips) and toss to coat.
Cover with plastic wrap and let marinate in the refrigerator for ~{30%minutes}.

Bring a #large pot{} of water to boil over high heat and season generously with @kosher salt{}.
Prepare an #ice bath{} in a large bowl.
Blanch the @spinach{4%cups} in the boiling water for ~{30%seconds}, then transfer to the ice bath to shock, then drain. 
ransfer to a small bowl and season with @sesame oil{1%teaspoon}, @kosher salt{}, and @black pepper{}(freshly ground) to taste.

In a #medium skillet{}, heat @sesame oil{1%teaspoon} over medium heat.
Add the @carrots{2%large}(julienned) and cook until softened, ~{2-3%minutes}.
Remove from the pan and set aside. Season with @kosher salt{}.

In the same skillet, heat @sesame oil{1%tablespoon} over medium-high heat.
Add the @garlic{1%clove}(remaining, minced) and cook for ~{30%seconds}, until fragrant.
Add the @shiitake mushrooms{8%oz}(stems removed, thinly sliced) and cook,
stirring frequently, until softened, about ~{2%minutes}.
Season with @kosher salt{}, then remove from the pan and set aside.

In the same skillet, heat the remaining @sesame oil{1%tablespoon} over medium-high heat.
Add the marinated @chicken thighs{} and sauté, stirring occasionally, until cooked through, about ~{5%minutes}.

Heat a #nonstick pan{} over medium-high heat. Melt @butter{1%tablespoon} in the pan.
Once the foaming subsides, crack @eggs{2%large} into the pan and cook until the whites
are firm and golden brown around the edges and the yolks are still runny, or to your desired doneness.

To assemble the bibimbap bowls, top the @sushi rice{}(cooked) with the @chicken thighs{},
@cabbage kimchi{1%cup}, @scallions{1%bunch}(sliced on the bias), @carrots{}, @spinach{},
@shiitake mushrooms{}, @persian cucumber{1}(thinly sliced), and the fried @eggs{}.

Enjoy!

